
#Problem Statement
# A government tax portal calculates tax based on the following conditions:
# •
# Income up to ₹5,00,000 → No tax
# •
# ₹5,00,001 to ₹10,00,000 → 10%
# •
# ₹10,00,001 to ₹20,00,000 → 20%
# •
# Above ₹20,00,000 → 30%
# Additional Benefits:
# •
# Senior citizens (Age ≥ 60) receive a 5% rebate on tax.
# •
# Women taxpayers receive an additional 2% rebate on tax.
# Write a Python program to calculate the final tax amount payable.
#  Input details
income = float(input("Enter annual income (₹): "))
age = int(input("Enter age: "))
gender = input("Enter gender (Male/Female): ").strip().lower()

# Calculate tax based on income
if income <= 500000:
    tax = 0
elif income <= 1000000:
    tax = income * 0.10
elif income <= 2000000:
    tax = income * 0.20
else:
    tax = income * 0.30

# Apply senior citizen rebate (5%)
if age >= 60:
    tax = tax - (tax * 0.05)

# Apply women taxpayer rebate (2%)
if gender == "female":
    tax = tax - (tax * 0.02)

# Display final tax
print(f"Final Tax Payable: ₹{tax:.2f}")


